      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's completely understandable to feel skeptical about therapy when you already feel so controlled by the system. Sometimes, the goal isn't just to \"process\" things, but to find moments of genuine agency within the overwhelming structure. Even small acts of rebellion against the routine—a different path to work, a new hobby, or changing how you view your downtime—can chip away at that feeling of being a mere function. You don't have to find one grand solution; sometimes the power is in the tiny choices you make each day.",
      "source": "target",
